You are absolutely right. It is contradictory to tell the user "You will be notified once it is created" and then immediately say "Batch created successfully" in the exact same pop-up!
Since the actual success or failure will be pushed to the user via the Notification Bell, the Snackbar should purely act as an informational message that the request was accepted by the system.
Here is the exact replacement for that section in your **Frontend** (JournalPosting.js).
### Update the Submit Snackbar Message
Find your handleSubmit function (around line 265). We will change the message to perfectly match your request and change the color to blue ("info") since it is an informational notice, not the final success.
**Find this exact block:**
```javascript
      showSnackBar(
        `Your request has been initiated. You will be notified once the batch is Created/Failed. Batch created successfully with Batch ID : ${newBatchId}`,
        "success"
      );
      setRows([{ ...initialRowState, id: Date.now() }]);
      setCommonBatchRemarks("");
      setChecked(false);
      setBranchInputValues({});
      setCglInputValues({});
    } catch (error) {
      // Safely grab the backend error message if available
      const errMsg = error?.response?.data?.message || error.message || "System error occurred.";
      showSnackBar(`Batch creation failed: ${errMsg}`, "error");
    } finally {
      setIsSubmitting(false);
    }
  };

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
      // We don't need to show the ID here anymore, just the informational warning
      showSnackBar(
        "Your Request has been initiated. You will be Notified once the Batch is Created/Failed.",
        "info"
      );
      
      setRows([{ ...initialRowState, id: Date.now() }]);
      setCommonBatchRemarks("");
      setChecked(false);
      setBranchInputValues({});
      setCglInputValues({});
    } catch (error) {
      // If it fails instantly (e.g. server down, bad network), show an error snackbar
      const errMsg = error?.response?.data?.message || error.message || "System error occurred.";
      showSnackBar(`Failed to initiate request: ${errMsg}`, "error");
    } finally {
      setIsSubmitting(false);
    }
  };

```
**Why this is better:**
 1. **No Contradictions:** The user gets a clear blue info popup telling them their job is done and the system has taken over.
 2. **Notification Driven:** They will now naturally look at their Notification Bell to see the final "Batch created Successfully with Batch ID : 00056" message that we configured in the backend!
